First, the problem is that in the HTML‐markup grammar we were treating *any* quote character inside an attribute value as “punctuation,” so nested quotes in something like

    <google-chart data='[["Month","Days"],["Jan",31]]'></google-chart>

end up being highlighted as punctuation. What we really want is to only highlight the *wrapper* quotes around the attribute value, not every quote inside it.

To fix this, we need to tighten up the two occurrences of

    /"|'/

in the `punctuation` lists under `attr-value` so that they only match quotes at the *start* or *end* of the value, i.e. `/^["']|["']$/`, instead of literally every quote character.

